sinfo: add the gc5603 to the T41 sensor table

sinfo is what identifies the sensor when the u-boot environment does not name
one, and its table has no gc5603, so on an untouched T41NQ camera
/proc/jz/sinfo/info answers "sensor not found". load_ingenic then ends up with
an empty SENSOR and asks modprobe for "sensor__t41", which does not exist: the
camera boots with no image and nothing explains why.

Every field is taken from this repository's own gc5603 driver, so the entry
cannot drift from the driver that will bind, and all of it is confirmed against
the camera's boot log:

  address    0x31            sensors/t41/gc5603/gc5603.c: .cbus_device = 0x31
                             "gc5603 chip found @ 0x31 (i2c0)"
  registers  0x03f0, 0x03f1  gc5603_detect() reads exactly these two
  values     0x56, 0x03      GC5603_CHIP_ID_H / _L, and the same pair appears in
                             the detect log lines
  clock      27 MHz          "sensor mclk 27000000 Hz"

The entry goes at the head of the table rather than into the CONFIG_SOC_T41
block at its tail, because probing is sequential and every candidate costs a
clock setup, a reset pulse and a couple of i2c reads. From the tail, behind 103
sensors that this SoC cannot have, a successful detection took over ten seconds
on the camera; from the head it is immediate. The block is compiled out
everywhere else, so no other SoC sees any change in probe order - which is why
the existing tail block is left exactly where it is rather than moved.

The mclk_name column is carried over from its neighbours for consistency only:
sinfo overwrites it at run time, taking "div_cim" and reparenting "mux_cim" to
vpll under CONFIG_SOC_T41 && CONFIG_KERNEL_4_4_94, so the value written here is
never used on this SoC.

Signed-off-by: Oskari Rauta <oskari.rauta@gmail.com>

--- a/kernel/sinfo/sensor_info.c
+++ b/kernel/sinfo/sensor_info.c
@@ -115,6 +115,9 @@
 
 SENSOR_INFO_T g_sinfo[] =
 {
+#ifdef CONFIG_SOC_T41
+	{"gc5603", 0x31,  "cgu_cim", 27000000, {0x56, 0x03}, 1, {0x03f0, 0x03f1}, 2, 2, NULL},
+#endif
 	{"ar0130", 0x10,  "cgu_cim", 24000000, {0x2402}, 2, {0x3000}, 2, 1, NULL},
 	{"ar0237", 0x10,  "cgu_cim", 27000000, {0x0256}, 2, {0x3000}, 2, 1, NULL},
 	{"bf3115", 0x6e,  "cgu_cim", 24000000, {0x31, 0x16}, 1, {0xfc, 0xfd}, 1, 2, NULL},
